From 436551e45306c144cc382393301eb1c57111d1a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:31:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/36] Restore Qt4 ifdefs removed in af84b80c and e76c8774

Revert af84b80c (Qt4-specific #if QT_VERSION guards across ~86 files)
and e76c8774 (QAIM_reset.h, the beginResetModel()/reset() wrapper),
resolved against the current v0.7 tree: 20 files had diverged enough
since v0.6 to conflict and needed manual resolution rather than a
clean auto-merge.

Notable resolution decisions:
- Several conflicts were genuine v0.7-era feature/API changes
  unrelated to Qt4 (async PasswordDialog API in ComposeWidget.cpp/
  Window.cpp, QLineEdit::addAction(..., LeadingPosition) in
  MessageListWidget.cpp, restructured Envelope/AddressRowWidget
  escaping, TROJITA_HAS_QNETWORKSESSION removal in
  SystemNetworkWatcher.cpp); kept the v0.7 behavior and only bolted
  on the missing Qt4 code path instead of reverting to v0.6 wholesale.
- Consolidated the ad hoc "#if QT_VERSION < 5 ? Qt::escape : X.toHtmlEscaped()"
  duplication onto the existing UiUtils::Formatting::htmlEscaped()
  helper (already dual-Qt internally) instead of re-adding per-site
  guards, for the handful of sites touched by these two reverts.
- LineEdit lost its self-drawn clear button in favor of Qt 5.2's
  QLineEdit::setClearButtonEnabled(); restored the Qt4 QToolButton
  implementation (init/clearButton/updateClearButton/sizeHint) under
  a version guard, and converted its lambda connect to a named slot
  in the process since the surrounding code was already being touched.
- Restored the Qt4 static-plugin export pattern's prerequisite bits
  in the three surviving plugin headers (Q_PLUGIN_METADATA now
  Qt5-only; Q_INTERFACES kept pointing at v0.7's current, more
  specific interfaces rather than v0.6's).
